<title>SWITZERLAND: Norway central bank head not concerned about crown.</title>
<headline>Norway central bank head not concerned about crown.</headline>
<dateline>BASLE, Switzerland 1997-04-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Norwegian Central Bank Governor Kjell Storvik said he was not concerned about the recent decline of the Norwegian crown on foreign exchange markets.</p>
<p>Asked by reporters whether he was concerned about the crown's recent fall, Storvik said: &quot;No, no.&quot;</p>
<p>Storvik did not elaborate.</p>
<p>He was speaking to reporters at the Bank for International Settlements, before a regular meeting here of G10 central bank governors here.</p>
<p>-- Zurich Editorial, +41 1 631 7340</p>
</text>
